            {
              "id": "0c9dac94-3a02-3481-a866-2d1de101719c",
              "name": "Promise Without Catch Handler",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nUnhandled Promise Rejection Vulnerability in JavaScript occurs when a promise is rejected, but there is no error handling mechanism in place to catch and handle the error. This can lead to unexpected application behavior, including crashes, and can potentially expose sensitive information or allow for other security vulnerabilities to be exploited.\n\nIn the provided code, the promise returned by `db.User.find()` is not being properly handled. If the promise is rejected (for example, if there is a problem connecting to the database), the rejection will not be caught and handled, leading to an Unhandled Promise Rejection.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should always have a `.catch()` block for every `.then()` block in your promises. The `.catch()` block will catch any errors that occur in the promise chain and allow you to handle them appropriately.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is how you can fix the provided code:\n\n```javascript\ndb.User.find({\n\twhere: {\n\t\t'login': req.body.login\n\t}\n}).then(user => {\n\tif (user) {\n\t\t// Send reset link via email happens here\n\t\treq.flash('info', 'Check email for reset link')\n\t\tres.redirect('/login')\n\t} else {\n\t\treq.flash('danger', \"Invalid login username\")\n\t\tres.redirect('/forgotpw')\n\t}\n}).catch(err => {\n\t// Handle the error here\n\tconsole.error(err);\n\tres.status(500).send('An error occurred');\n});\n```\n\nIn this fixed code, a `.catch()` block has been added to handle any errors that occur when trying to find the user in the database.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code appears to require the following libraries:\n\n- A database library (such as Sequelize) to provide the `db.User.find()` function.\n- An Express.js-like library to provide the `req` and `res` objects.\n- A flash messaging library (such as connect-flash) to provide the `req.flash()` function.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP - Unhandled Promise Rejection](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Nodejs_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html#unhandled-promise-rejections)\n- [CWE-754: Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/754.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-754",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/754.html"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-754"
                ]
              }
